{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Behold, the hand of YHWH Havayah.</b> In this fifth plague He mentioned the hand of YHWH Havayah, which is the final ה of the Name, and He mentioned the expression Havayah, which is the last of the names from the combination of the special Name that bears twelve letters, as hinted in the verse ״זה שמי לעולם״, and He mentioned as well ה (five) species from the livestock. And understand this." "<b>Upon your livestock that are in the field.</b> He warned them in the present, for most livestock is in the field, in the manner of (Exodus 22:30): ״ובשר בשדה טרפה לא תאכלו״ — and you shall not eat torn flesh in the field — for even a torn animal indoors is forbidden, but the verse speaks of the usual case. So too here, for the matter affected even the indoor livestock, as it is written (Exodus 9:6): ״וימת כל מקנה מצרים״." "<b>But.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote that He specified ״that are in the field״ because all their livestock was in the field; they would never gather it into the houses, since ״תועבת מצרים כל רועה צאן״ — every shepherd is an abomination to the Egyptians — and because of this they kept them far from the cities. And so the livestock was far from the land of Egypt, in the field at the border of the land of Goshen, and everything was mixed together in the grazing place, the livestock of Egypt and the livestock of Israel. Therefore it was necessary to say ״והפלה ה' בין מקנה ישראל ובין מקנה מצרים״, or because the plague of pestilence comes from a change in the air, and the air was all the same in one place and at one time, and the corruption of the air should have spread also to the livestock of Israel, except that the Holy One, blessed be He, performed a miracle for them."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:15.029363734Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}